New tests worth naming:

    test_summary_links_resolve_to_anchors_that_exist
        every `detail` link in the summary points at an anchor that exists,
        and no anchor is reused. A link that lands nowhere is worse than none.
    test_a_second_turn_is_not_treated_as_already_closed
        the close marker is per turn. Scanning the whole document for it would
        make every turn after the first silently skip its own result.
    test_the_transcript_the_evals_read_is_untouched
        `evals/harness.py::_turn_telemetry` counts rounds and tool_calls out of
        `.shamsu/sessions/*/messages.jsonl`. Asserts (2, 2) after a full turn
        writes the new logs into the same workspace.
    test_reasoning_is_a_sub_panel_inside_the_model_entry
        trace renders BEFORE the response, inside <details>, in the same block.
    test_inline_thought_tags_are_pulled_out_of_the_answer
        a leaked `<think>` block lands in the panel, not in front of the answer.
    test_simple_mode_records_its_tools_and_model_calls
        drives a real SimpleChatLoop with a scripted client and asserts the
        tool row, the model row, and the reasoning all reach the log. This is
        finding 1 above, held down.


EVAL SAFETY
-----------
`messages.jsonl` is untouched by this refactor — no code in it was changed and
`_turn_telemetry` reads the same file the same way. Covered by
`test_the_transcript_the_evals_read_is_untouched`, which writes a transcript,
runs a full turn that produces the new logs beside it, and asserts the counts
still come back (2, 2).


DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE BRIEF
------------------------------------
1. `.evidence/` KEPT ITS JSONL FILES. The brief said a session should "just"
   contain the two Markdown files, session.json, messages.jsonl and
   attachments/. `events.jsonl`, `decisions.jsonl`, `tool-calls.jsonl`,
   `model-calls.jsonl` and `manifest.json` stayed, because
   `ActionLedger.evidence_outcome()` computes every run's terminal status from
   them and `store.py` validates runs against them. Deleting them would have
   made every run's status wrong. What was fragmented — and what is now one
   folder — is the eight typed SUBFOLDERS.

2. `essential` vs `verbose` MOVED ITS LINE. With one document, `essential` had
   to withhold the model's own words to stay readable. With two, the summary
   stays skimmable on its own, so the response and the reasoning trace are now
   kept at BOTH levels — they are what you debug a small model with. `verbose`
   still adds the prompt that was sent and the context payload.
   See `test_essential_detail_keeps_the_answer_and_drops_the_prompt`.

3. `report.md` IS GONE, not kept alongside. `store.report_path()` now returns
   the session's `log-summary.md`, falling back to a run's own `report.md` (or
   the older `narrative.md`) when it exists, so `/run report` and the headless
   result keep working on runs recorded before today.


